        this(name); // call the constructor that takes a String argument
        this.age = age;
    }

    // getters and setters
}
```

In the example above, the constructor that takes two arguments (name and age) calls the constructor that takes only one argument (name) as its first statement using the `this` keyword. This allows the `name` component to be initialized before the `age` component.

